From 6599adf3c7341eaa2a36af6600136324bd732ef8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:02:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(db): transform the vendor OSV records into distro-keyed
 affected packages

Add the vendor OSV strategy for BELL-* records: every affected entry
becomes an apk affected package carrying the OperatingSystem derived from
the ecosystem string ("<family>:23" -> <os-release id> 23,
"<family>:stream" -> <os-release id>, label "stream"), so the apk matcher
reaches it through its distro search. Ranges keep the apk notation and the
apk comparator; multi-window constraints are emitted comma-separated, which
the generic constraint parser requires. The rewrite is local to the
strategy (vendorRanges); the shared helpers and the output of every other
strategy are unchanged. The CVE is taken from the record id
(BELL-CVE-2025-59375 -> CVE-2025-59375) and from aliases/related; the OSV
model vendored here has no upstream[] field.

The apk matcher tests drive real vendor records
(grype/matcher/apk/testdata/vendor-apk): per-release ranges, origin
indirection, fixed-version ignores, and isolation in both directions
between BELL-* records and Alpine / Wolfi packages.

Ported from the database part of #3264.
